{
  "id": "Lyo.Scheduler.Cache",
  "name": "Lyo.Scheduler.Cache",
  "area": "Core",
  "tagline": "Cache-backed `ISchedulerStateStore` for `Lyo.Scheduler`. Persists each schedule's `LastRunUtc` / `NextRunUtc` / state markers through `Lyo.Cache` so cron/interval/one-shot schedules survive process…",
  "description": "Cache-backed `ISchedulerStateStore` for [`Lyo.Scheduler`](../Lyo.Scheduler/README.md). Persists each schedule's `LastRunUtc` / `NextRunUtc` / state markers through [\n`Lyo.Cache`](../../Cache/Lyo.Cache/README.md) so cron/interval/one-shot schedules survive process restarts without external infrastructure beyond whatever backs your cache (Fusion\nin-memory, Postgres, Redis, …).",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register with DI",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "using Lyo.Scheduler.Cache;\n\n// Register cache first (e.g. via Lyo.Cache.Fusion):\nservices.AddFusionCache(); // or whichever ICacheService registration suits the host\n\n// Then register the scheduler with cache persistence:\nservices.AddSchedulerWithCache(o =>\n{\n    o.CheckIntervalMs = 5_000;\n});"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Types",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Role"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**`CacheSchedulerStateStore`**",
          "`ISchedulerStateStore` implementation that reads and writes scheduler state through `ICacheService`. Keys are scoped per schedule id."
        ],
        [
          "**`SchedulerCacheExtensions`**",
          "DI extensions."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "DI",
      "text": "`AddSchedulerWithCache` is a convenience over `services.AddScheduler(sp => new CacheSchedulerStateStore(sp.GetRequiredService<ICacheService>()), ...)`. It requires `ICacheService` to be registered beforehand."
    }
  ],
